# Felidar Retreat, second mode: "Put a +1/+1 counter on each creature you control. Those creatures gain vigilance until end of turn."
# (CR 122.1, 611.2c, 702.20.) Bot1 casts the Retreat on turn 1 (Black Lotus WWW and Mox Jet, exactly {3}{W}) with a Memnite out. On turn 2 Bot2
# plays a Memnite and an Island: the Island is not "a land you control" for Bot1, so nothing triggers. On turn 3 Bot1's Plains triggers it
# and the counter mode makes Bot1's Memnite a 2/2 with vigilance, leaves Bot2's Memnite a 1/1 without it ("you control"), and an
# Ornithopter cast afterwards gets neither (the creatures are fixed as the ability resolves). On turn 4 the counter stays and the vigilance is gone.

